      "checks": [
        {"space": "save-block-1", "offset": "0x10E0", "type": "u32le", "equals": "0xE8F828BC"},
        {"space": "save-block-1", "offset": "0x0000", "type": "u16le", "equals": 5}
      ],
      "source": "engine:src/PKHeX.Everywhere.RomHacks/Expansion/HeartAndSoul/HeartAndSoulFormat.cs and engine:src/PKHeX.Everywhere.RomHacks/Expansion/HeartAndSoul/HeartAndSoulSave.cs",
      "note": "Heart & Soul keeps Emerald's signature, so its magic tells its saves apart. The engine claims a save with the magic and refuses one whose save version isn't 5, so this doesn't match those. The engine reads the slot with the higher counter, without gen3-slots' wrap from 0xFFFFFFFF to 0, so the two can read different slots of a save whose counter has wrapped."
    }
  },
  "note": "Pokémon Heart & Soul is built on pokeemerald-expansion. It keeps Emerald's two slots of 14 sections, but its checksums cover other lengths, and each section's bytes after them hold SaveBlock3. SaveBlock1 starts with the save version, so the party sits 4 bytes later than Emerald's. Its Pokémon pack wider fields into the Gen 3 substructures. 2.0 is Release-v2.0.6, whose saves have version 5.",
